-> HAS_FACET [node:8a6a1300-bb21-4ae1-8d79-4957f245fc99] @ 2026-09-08T09:36:59.039273+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:d2844438-9992-4e20-bfb5-fa615a906574] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:13.543921+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:36:59.039273+00:00

The kiosk runs on an A8X with 2 GB RAM on a display that is never asleep, so per-frame cost is a design constraint rather than an optimisation: animate opacity and transform only (never box-shadow, filter, backdrop-filter, width or height), keep backdrop-filter to a single 4px use on the slideshow and dialog scrim rather than per card, and do not ship translucent card surfaces, soft shadows or default scanlines - each costs a full-screen composite.
---
