path: /artifact/the-kitchen-terminal-is-read-from-three
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:36:59.157308+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:68773fd1-2296-4527-b027-8d5d6c699ece] @ 2026-09-08T09:36:59.157308+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:73fb6132-40d3-4e2d-8b88-334442c4bfa7] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:09.546289+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:36:59.157308+00:00

The kitchen terminal is read from three distances - the doorway at 3 m, the counter at 1 m, and the glass at 0.4 m with wet hands - and the whole visual system is derived from them. Type is two tiers: a read tier for anything you walk up to and a glance tier for what must survive the doorway, sized by subtended x-height (comfortable at 5 arcmin, glanceable at 8). Body text is 20px, not 16; the wireframes' 11-13px is a desktop habit and is the single largest correction to the accepted wireframes.
---
