-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:45.914819+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:d8f13deb-0013-41b1-9f8c-a57918a3b130] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:45.914819+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:45.914819+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f96f62c3-d72a-4c40-8e16-57278ca1f302] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:45.914819+00:00

The layout schema uses the bare word grid for two different things - the column grid a layout's own cards flow into, and a container card type whose cells are all visible at once - so the domain model names them apart as DashboardGrid and CardGrid. The schema file itself is unchanged; the disambiguation is in the language, and code, tests and UI copy use the two names rather than the overloaded one.
