-> CONTRADICTS [node:b6cc5895-5e52-462a-aab2-c934ba921825] @ 2026-09-08T14:55:08.289479+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T14:55:08.289479+00:00

TypeScript 7 with the native Go compiler is generally available - 7.0.2 on npm - so the plan's assumption that it would exist has held, and the verification it asked for is done. Vite 8, Svelte 5, Astro 7 and Fastify 5 are likewise all real releases, so nothing in the assumed stack is aspirational. What does not follow, and was wrongly claimed here at first, is that scaffolding can therefore use 7: the compiler shipped ahead of its ecosystem, and the pin is 6.x.
---
