path: /artifact/varlock-treats-every-value-as-sensitive
created_at: 2026-09-08T15:18:34.915005+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:c3dc31be-39b3-4422-a4f6-41136bfb48aa] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:34.915005+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:34.915005+00:00

Varlock treats every value as sensitive unless explicitly marked public - defaultSensitive is true project-wide - and real secret values never live in the committed schema file, only in a git-ignored local env file or a secret provider. The schema declares shape and sensitivity so agents can read it safely; an agent that helpfully fills a value into it has published a credential. This project's schema sets defaultSensitive false in the header and then marks each of the three secrets sensitive individually, so the marking stays correct even if someone later edits or removes that header default.
---
