-> ABOUT [node:49ba726c-031e-4a01-839f-11a76a8bf009] @ 2026-09-09T05:38:22.879032+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:79662ce5-7b55-458a-b0e9-f0efd406d5a8] @ 2026-09-09T05:38:23.003761+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-09T05:38:22.879032+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-09T05:38:22.879032+00:00

Every card carries a shared shell component rather than its own copy of the card chrome. The shell is an ordinary Svelte component and not a second custom element, because slotting content across two shadow roots is the fiddly way to compose them and buys nothing here - each widget is already its own custom element. The reason it matters beyond tidiness is the token contract: the checker can only prove that no component hardcodes a colour if the chrome those components share lives in exactly one file, and thirteen copies of the card frame would be thirteen places for a hex literal to appear.
---
