-> HAS_FACET [node:8a6a1300-bb21-4ae1-8d79-4957f245fc99] @ 2026-09-09T05:57:27.612002+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-09T05:57:27.612002+00:00

The kiosk sizes itself with a percentage height chained from the root element and never with viewport units. Each unit fails differently here: 100vh is wrong in a standalone PWA on iOS because the toolbar is gone and the unit does not know; dvh, svh and lvh are Safari 15.4 and past the floor, and the token-contract check fails a build that ships them; vw includes the scrollbar width, so sizing to it is a way to cause the horizontal scrollbar it was meant to avoid. Worst of the four was the usual iOS workaround: height set to webkit-fill-available resolves against a parent that has no height of its own and measured 887 pixels inside a 768 pixel viewport, overriding the 100vh it was supposed to back up, so the fallback added for one browser was the overflow in every browser. A height of 100 percent has no such ambiguity once html carries a height.
---
[node:26582685-718f-4003-9454-5126ff416a15]
type: constraint
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/the-card-deck-fits-by-construction-rathe
created_at: 2026-09-09T05:57:27.730936+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:7108856c-d3d5-4701-bb69-11087256a081] @ 2026-09-09T05:57:27.967751+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-09T05:57:27.730936+00:00

The card deck fits by construction rather than by scrolling. Rows are minmax(0, 1fr) and each grid item carries min-height zero, because a grid item's automatic minimum size is its content and that silently defeats fractional rows; the deck then clips instead of scrolling, and the page has overflow hidden so a scrollbar anywhere means a bug rather than a feature. This releases the minimum card height inside the deck, and that is not a loss: the token existed so rows would not jump as data loads, and equal fractional rows give the stronger version of the same guarantee, because row height stops depending on content at all. On a wall display nobody is present to scroll, so content below the fold is content that does not exist.
---
