[node:2946e332-fd2b-4b23-9f13-a6f014255945]
type: constraint
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/the-microphone-is-never-requested-when-a
created_at: 2026-09-09T06:22:37.815060+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:49ba726c-031e-4a01-839f-11a76a8bf009] @ 2026-09-09T06:22:37.815060+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c3dc31be-39b3-4422-a4f6-41136bfb48aa] @ 2026-09-09T06:22:37.815060+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-09T06:22:37.815060+00:00

The microphone is never requested when a card mounts. A wall kiosk has nobody standing at it to answer a permission prompt, so a card that asks on load renders as permanently dead and the household learns to ignore it. The audiometer shows an explicit off state with one control that asks, a pending state while the browser decides, and a named failure with a way to retry when permission is refused or no device exists. The stream and the audio context are released in the teardown, because a kiosk that holds the microphone open forever is both a battery cost and a thing a household should not have to trust.
---
