[node:fb55b3b0-5070-48a0-bd21-2168d12a92d5]
type: constraint
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/an-unresolved-css-custom-property-is-sil
created_at: 2026-09-09T06:55:32.816652+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:73fb6132-40d3-4e2d-8b88-334442c4bfa7] @ 2026-09-09T06:55:32.816652+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:79662ce5-7b55-458a-b0e9-f0efd406d5a8] @ 2026-09-09T06:55:33.215702+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-09T06:55:32.816652+00:00

An unresolved CSS custom property is silent. Nothing errors, nothing warns, and the declaration simply drops - so when the token sheet moved from a hand-written file to a generated one, five properties the components referenced stopped existing and the only symptom was body text losing its line height on a wall nobody was reading closely. Generation is therefore checked twice: the committed stylesheet is regenerated in CI and the build fails if it has drifted, and a test asserts that every var reference in the component sources appears as a declaration in the generated output. Runtime layout variables the renderer sets per page are excluded by name, because they are state travelling as custom properties rather than theme tokens.
---
[node:4a749051-6bc6-4807-bc52-47748e2bb914]
type: constraint
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/a-card-must-not-present-placeholder-data
created_at: 2026-09-09T06:55:32.953663+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:3c7e1fe3-fba9-48d1-b1f3-8dc9b463a550] @ 2026-09-09T06:55:32.953663+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:49ba726c-031e-4a01-839f-11a76a8bf009] @ 2026-09-09T06:55:32.953663+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-09T06:55:32.953663+00:00

A card must not present placeholder data as real. The calendar has no backend until OAuth2 exists, so it falls back to obviously-labelled sample events, says so in the card's meta, and stays at idle rather than ok - the state vocabulary already means something and ok would be a lie. The same reasoning that forbids a cache presenting stale data as current forbids a component presenting invented data as fetched, and a calendar is the worst card to be quietly wrong about because nobody double-checks what day it says a thing is on.
---
