-> ABOUT [node:15863232-0fb0-4c79-aaa9-3750ce8c0a2f] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:21.521930+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:4a749051-6bc6-4807-bc52-47748e2bb914] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:21.521930+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:21.521930+00:00

The recipe import HTTP contract is a two-step confirm flow rather than one endpoint: POST /api/recipes/import only extracts and returns an unsaved Recipe (id: ''), never writes to the database; a separate POST /api/recipes persists the (possibly user-edited) fields the review UI submits after the household approves them. This is what makes "review before save" real at the HTTP layer rather than only a UI convention — the server itself has no path that persists an unreviewed extraction.
---
