needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:56.315499+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:62d2072b-039e-439c-9dfa-1616e42a4afa] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:56.315499+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:ac006a24-2763-40e7-8423-2b851793efcf] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:56.315499+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c3dc31be-39b3-4422-a4f6-41136bfb48aa] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:56.315499+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f2e09a03-8e61-4299-ad7c-cef6c06775fe] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:56.315499+00:00

Chat routes never pass raw message content into Sentry.captureException's extra context or into log lines — only conversationId/model. This is how "chat transcripts must not leak into GlitchTip" is satisfied without stretching redact.ts's credential-pattern scrubbing over ordinary conversation text: conversation content isn't a credential shape, so pattern-matching it would either miss it entirely or, if forced, corrupt legitimate error diagnostics by over-redacting. The existing exact-value layer already covers the Kilo Gateway key itself via secretValues(); this decision covers the orthogonal case the key-scrubbing was never meant to handle.
---
