-> DEPENDS_ON [node:4730c1bc-b791-4a0d-a94c-1bd4f8307102] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:39.453435+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:39.453435+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:68b03a85-d372-45c5-80a4-549ebf826798] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:39.453435+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:8b9566f6-a1d5-4c43-952e-369c2796d5ca] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:39.453435+00:00
-> CONTRADICTS [node:8bfaa6ba-c432-44f9-a9f5-12aed72a8f15] @ 2026-09-09T12:04:49.777628+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f2e09a03-8e61-4299-ad7c-cef6c06775fe] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:39.453435+00:00

Compacting is implemented without new schema: the summary produced by the cheaper model is persisted as an ordinary Message with role='system' and content prefixed '[COMPACT] '. When ConversationService builds the working context window for a turn, it scans messages oldest-first and, if a '[COMPACT]'-prefixed system message exists, starts the window from the most recent one forward — older messages stay in the database untouched (visible in the full transcript) but are excluded from what is sent to the gateway. A hard rolling-window drop-oldest safety net (independent of compacting, re-checked after every drop) guarantees the gateway is never sent more than the model's context budget regardless of the token estimator's accuracy, since token counting uses a length/4 heuristic rather than a real tokenizer.
---
