-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-09T12:12:20.585019+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-09T12:12:20.585019+00:00

In a Svelte 5 component (.svelte file), instantiating the built-in `URLSearchParams` anywhere in the script — even purely locally, inside an async function, never touching component state — trips eslint-plugin-svelte's `svelte/prefer-svelte-reactivity` rule ("Use SvelteURLSearchParams instead"). The rule doesn't distinguish reactive from throwaway use. Fix used here: build query strings with manual template literals + encodeURIComponent instead (matching K7Weather.svelte's existing convention), rather than adding SvelteURLSearchParams or suppressing the rule.
