-> HAS_FACET [node:ccc18558-7181-44df-9608-de587d8d937c] @ 2026-09-10T04:32:34.085502+00:00

Kilo Gateway's model catalogue (368 models, fetched live 2026-09-10) has no Whisper-named or "transcription"-named model, but 33 models declare "audio" in architecture.input_modalities (chat-completion multimodal models: google/gemini-3.x-flash family, meta/muse-spark, thinkingmachines/inkling, nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni, openai/gpt-audio, etc). Three are free: thinkingmachines/inkling-small:free, thinkingmachines/inkling:free, nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning:free. This means transcription on this gateway is most plausibly implemented by routing audio through an audio-input-capable chat model rather than a dedicated Whisper endpoint, and a free audio-input model is available as a sensible default for the transcribe route's model config (mirroring the chat card's kilo-auto/free default pattern) — though which model /audio/transcriptions actually accepts could not be confirmed live (see the sibling issue node on the unverified contract).
