-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-10T04:32:39.576257+00:00

As of 2026-09-10, package.json has no multipart-body-parsing dependency (no @fastify/multipart, busboy, formidable) and src/server/index.ts registers no multipart or raw-body content-type parser — only fastify's built-in JSON body parsing is in use across every existing route (chat, recipes, etc). The chat-voice-input transcribe endpoint is the first route in this codebase that needs to accept binary audio, so it must either add @fastify/multipart or use Fastify's addContentTypeParser to accept a raw octet-stream/audio body directly (avoiding a new dependency) — the client can POST the MediaRecorder Blob's bytes with a real audio content-type (e.g. audio/webm) rather than wrapping it in multipart, since there is exactly one file per request and no other form fields are strictly needed (the model id can go in a query string or header instead).
---
