-> DEPENDS_ON [node:16b0ad21-fc54-45e2-aada-d2bac35f6ce2] @ 2026-09-10T04:35:50.844022+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-10T04:35:50.844022+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:68b03a85-d372-45c5-80a4-549ebf826798] @ 2026-09-10T04:35:50.844022+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:8b9566f6-a1d5-4c43-952e-369c2796d5ca] @ 2026-09-10T04:35:50.844022+00:00

k7-chat-voice-input's server transcribe route (POST /api/chat/transcribe) accepts a raw audio body (not multipart) from the client via a Fastify addContentTypeParser matching /^audio\// as a buffer, with bodyLimit raised to 10MB for that route — deliberately avoiding @fastify/multipart since there's exactly one file per request and no other form fields, and this is the first route in the codebase needing binary upload [node:16b0ad21]. The server itself then builds the multipart/form-data request Kilo Gateway's /audio/transcriptions endpoint is assumed to need, using Node's global FormData/Blob (no new dependency) — client-to-K7-server is raw bytes, K7-server-to-gateway is multipart.
---
