-> HAS_FACET [node:8a6a1300-bb21-4ae1-8d79-4957f245fc99] @ 2026-09-10T04:36:05.591766+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-10T04:36:05.591766+00:00

k7-chat-voice-input's client picks the MediaRecorder mime type at runtime via MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported against a candidate list (audio/webm;codecs=opus, audio/webm, audio/mp4, audio/mp4;codecs=mp4a.40.2), falling back to the browser default if none match, and uploads with the recorder's actual reported mimeType — deliberately not hardcoding audio/webm as the original task brief assumed. Safari's MediaRecorder does not reliably support WebM containers the way Chromium's does (it typically produces audio/mp4/AAC), and Safari 15 on the iPad Air 2 is this project's actual deployment target [node:0bc7e618], so a hardcoded webm/opus assumption would likely have shipped broken on the real device.
---
