-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-10T04:36:10.119002+00:00

k7-chat-voice-input's K7Chat.svelte mic control follows the K7Audiometer.svelte permission pattern exactly [node:2946e332]: feature-detected once (MediaRecorder + getUserMedia existence check) so showMic is false and the button never renders on an unsupported browser rather than rendering-then-breaking; getUserMedia is only ever called from the click handler, never on mount/effect; the MediaStream's tracks are stopped immediately after recording stops (before the network call), and the component's existing unmount $effect is extended to also tear down any live stream/recorder. Errors reuse the composer's existing failed/errorText display rather than a new UI region.
