-> ABOUT [node:441547c8-c8df-41c9-86d0-eebe5da729de] @ 2026-09-10T04:39:31.781331+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-10T04:39:14.650881+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-10T04:39:14.650881+00:00

Menu-to-target visibility coordination is necessarily page-level, living in main.ts rather than inside K7Menu.svelte: the menu component only knows its own items and dispatches a bubbling+composed CustomEvent('k7-menu-change', {detail:{cardId}}); main.ts (which alone has the full items list from card.params and can call document.getElementById) listens and toggles the native `hidden` attribute on every other target. This matches layout.yaml's real menu-kuchnia usage (audiometr/minutnik-kuchnia each keep their own separate grid slot; the menu hides one, CSS Grid auto-placement reflows around the gap) rather than inventing a shared-single-slot container the schema prose gestures at but no layout file exercises - flagged for human confirmation in the PR.
---
